From f0e27ef9b37432d78921dee9ef6df3bad3703e3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 18:19:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Costume storage, the wardrobe and the mounted glory

Three of the ops the furniture round left unanswered.

THE TREASURE CHEST is OSRS costume storage, done the way this repo already
does storage: a perm inv and a chat menu, no new interface, exactly like the
herb sack and the looting bag. Store takes one of each treasure trail reward
you are carrying, Check lists what is in it by set, and Take out withdraws a
whole set - which is how OSRS withdraws from costume storage, and also the
only way to pick one of 72 items out of a chat menu. Capacity runs 18 / 36 /
54 / 72 by tier.

The 72 are derived, and re-derived by the battery on every run. Two rules
decide membership: every god, gold-trimmed, trimmed and heraldic clue reward
is in it, matched by name; and nothing in it is stocked by any shop, which is
the half that covers the seventeen costume pieces no name pattern describes.
A costume is something clues are the only source of. That second rule is what
keeps this from drifting into a second bank one plausible item at a time.

THE WARDROBE opens the character-design screen, and shares its close handler
with the tutorial - there can only be one, a second is a build error. That
handler set %tutorial unconditionally, so the first time a finished player
opened a wardrobe their tutorial state would have been knocked back to 1. It
now only advances a player who is still in the tutorial.

THE MOUNTED GLORY gives the four amulet destinations without charges. Those
were written inside a label that ends by eating a charge off whatever is in
last_slot - from a loc trigger that is whatever the player is holding, so it
would have quietly rewritten an inventory slot. The choice and the teleport
are a proc now and the label eats the charge itself. The instance is freed on
the way out, or it holds a slot until logout.

It first went into poh_tablets.rs2, which is generated, and the next run
deleted it. Check 43 caught that - the second time in two days.

rs2check 0 ERROR / 0 CHECK; poh_battery ALL PASS (55 groups);
poh_mutate 101/101 caught.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J1qUhTcu63bJ3hCBBxy7nU
